From: Khem Raj <raj.khem@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 07:25:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 3rdparty/open62541: use ASN1_STRING accessors for the SAN URI

ASN1_IA5STRING is an alias for the ASN1_STRING type (struct
asn1_string_st), which became opaque in OpenSSL 4.0 - it is no longer
defined in any public header - so reading its members directly stops
compiling:

  open62541.c:122174:56: error: incomplete definition of type 'ASN1_IA5STRING' (aka 'struct asn1_string_st')
   122174 |              subjectURI.length = (size_t) (value->d.ia5->length);
  open62541.c:122182:58: error: incomplete definition of type 'ASN1_IA5STRING' (aka 'struct asn1_string_st')
   122182 |              (void) memcpy (subjectURI.data, value->d.ia5->data, subjectURI.length);

Use ASN1_STRING_length() and ASN1_STRING_get0_data() instead. Both are
public accessors that OpenSSL has provided since 1.1.0, and they return
exactly the members being read here, so behaviour is unchanged.

This only breaks the target build, not qtopcua-native: the open62541
PACKAGECONFIG that pulls this plugin in is empty for the native and
nativesdk variants.

Upstream-Status: Pending [the same code is still present upstream in
open62541 itself, plugins/crypto/openssl/certificategroup.c, from which
this amalgamated source is generated; qtopcua carries it as a vendored
copy under src/3rdparty/open62541]
Signed-off-by: Khem Raj <raj.khem@gmail.com>
